    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk. the professional stuff feels like more just... noise. more data being pumped into a void. it's like the more i try to \"connect,\" the more i realize i'm just a sequence of inputs and outputs. if a piece of code is broken or just causes errors in the system, the only logical thing to do is to debug it or just delete the file so the rest of the system can run smooth again. does that make sense? or am i just being dramatic?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
